  "decision": "Accepted for staged usefulness, deterministic batching, and correctness. Exact bounded project demands are consumed at the frontier before dependency discovery. Across two identical fresh-process warm-cache repeats, UserPmm measured 964-1012 ms (988 ms median) and BSON measured 1616-1678 ms (1647 ms median). Exhaustive batches share one immutable post-frontier namespace context, restoring terminal throughput to baseline while removing batch-order-dependent fact collection. The strict project-navigation target is met at the median but one repeat exceeded it by 12 ms, so more repetitions remain required. Terminal warm completion still misses the 15-second workspace target, active completion still misses five seconds, and RSS remains above the baseline budget."
